kind: vulnerability
title: "n8n fixes five critical flaws that let a workflow editor run code or read files on the server, CVE-2026-42231 and four more"
headline: "Five n8n flaws let a user who can edit workflows run code on the server or read its files; fixed in April and May"
summary: "n8n published five critical advisories (each CVSS 4.0 9.4) in April and May 2026. Prototype-pollution flaws in the webhook XML parser (CVE-2026-42231), the XML node (CVE-2026-42232, with a fix bypass CVE-2026-44791) and HTTP Request pagination (CVE-2026-44789) can lead to code execution, and a Git node flag injection (CVE-2026-44790) allows file read. All five need a user with permission to create or modify workflows; versions 1.123.43, 2.20.7 and 2.22.1 carry the later fixes."
event_date: 2026-05-13
